WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
By the 1940s, scientists knew that
chromosomes contain two things:

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.310
DNA and protein.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.830
Protein is built from
20 kinds of amino acid.

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.400
DNA has just 4 bases, on
a backbone that repeats.

5
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:20.330
To many scientists, DNA looked
far too simple to carry the genes.

6
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.530
So how can just four kinds of base hold
the instructions for a whole organism?

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.410
In this mission, you'll find where in
the molecule the information really sits.

8
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.260
Then you'll see how base pairing
lets that information be copied,

9
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.440
and carried to the ribosomes.

10
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:41.670
Your mission: explain how four kinds of
base can hold the instructions for a whole

11
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.530
organism.
